<div className={styles.pvlRoot}>
	<div style="background-color:;display:block !important;" class="p-6 rounded-5 bg-light mb-18" data-zesty-id="design:columns:1 Column:51:34">
<div style="flex:1" className={styles.pvlColumn} class="column" data-zesty-id="design:columns:1 Column:51:34-1:1 Column:0">
<img width="305" height="296" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/uss-cache.salvationarmy.org/10e9509e-253d-4f22-be2b-5a514d7ebf42_Majors+Ricky+and+Karla+Perez.jpg" alt="placeholder" class="img-fluid d-block my-3 mx-auto" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;" loading="lazy" / data-zesty-id="content:images:1:7">
<div class="my-2" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-sm:3:92"></div>
<h5 style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:text:4:46">Majors Karla and Ricky Perez</h5>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:5:61">
	<span><span lang="en-US">Majors Karla and Ricky Perez&nbsp;arrived in Hickory June of 2024.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span>
</p>
<div class="py-5" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-xl:6:87"></div>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:7:67">Major Ricky Perez was born in Rochester, NY. He grew up in New York and Florida. He is</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:8:98">working on a Christian Ministry degree with Trevecca Nazarene University.</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:9:35">Major Karla Perez was born in Santurce, Puerto Rico. She moved to the United States when</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:10:32">she was 10 years old and grew up in Florida. She has a bachelor’s degree in Christian</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:11:1">Ministry from Trevecca Nazarene University and a master’s degree in clinical Mental Health</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:12:31">Counseling from Liberty University.</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:13:69">They got married on March 10, 2001, in Florida. They felt the call to become Officers and</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:14:12">entered The Salvation Army training college in 2003 and graduated in 2005. Upon&nbsp;</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:15:4">graduation, they were sent back home to serve in Florida. While in Florida, they served in</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:16:16">the following commands: Orlando, Stuart, Daytona Beach, Winter Haven, and Naples.</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:17:89">After 13 years of serving in the Sunshine State of Florida, they were sent out of Florida for</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:18:33">the first time when they were appointed to Durham, NC in 2018, where they served for 6</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:19:13">years.&nbsp;</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:20:75">They have 3 children. Ke’olani (19) attends Asbury University in Wilmore, KY. Their two</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:21:86">youngest sons are Josiah (16) and Ezekiel (14). Major Ricky enjoys spending time in the</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:22:97">outdoors, fishing, hunting, kayaking, cycling, and playing golf. Major Karla enjoys spending</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:23:88">time in nature, scrapbooking, crafting, and reading.</p>
<p class="MsoBodyText3" style="text-align:center;" data-zesty-id="content:textarea:24:14">They are looking forward for all that God has in store for their time in Hickory!</p>
<div class="py-5" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-xl:25:95"></div>
